// us.irs.rev_rul_6621_quarterly — the IRS Revenue Rulings publishing the
// quarterly interest rates of 26 U.S.C. §6621.
//
// WHY A PACKAGE. Five coverage rows (payment-refunds-interest.json:
// 26/6621/b/u1, 26/6621/b/1/u1, 26/6621/b/2/a/u1, 26/6621/b/2/b/u1,
// 26/6621/b/3/u1 — all SOURCE_GAP) read the federal short-term rate —
// the Secretary-determined quarterly figure under §1274(d), published in
// the IRB Rev. Rul. series. No row names concrete quarters: owners need
// the quarterly contract «short-term rate(quarter T) → figure» plus
// anchored quarters, not the archive. One ruling names the §6621(b) input
// explicitly: the §1274(d) rate for the determination month (first month
// of the preceding quarter), rounded to the nearest full percent on daily
// compounding (Notice 88-59), and restates the §6621(a) spreads verbatim.
//
// WHAT IT HOLDS (phase 1, still rule-less). `sources/*.pdf` — the
// official IRS bytes, pinned by sha256 (`sources/provenance.json`: URL,
// bytes, sha256, last-modified, quarter→ruling — no rate values). Whole
// issues as carriers, byte-exact as published: two standalone Rev. Rul.
// PDFs (irs-drop) and two full IRB issues (irs-irbs; no standalone
// drop-PDF exists for Rev. Rul. 2026-5 and 2026-10). Ruling slices come
// later, on the old-PL scheme. `sources.law` +
// `sources/tables/quarterly-2026.lawtable.json` — the four 2026 quarters
// as structure (quarter/tier → Decimal share, 24 anchored rows) with
// quote-anchored fragments, plus `quarter-index.json` (quarter →
// ruling/table/edition). All of it GENERATED by
// `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irs_6621_quarterly.py`, never
// hand-edited. No rules: the value, its quarter and its reading belong
// to the owner, the rate entering the case as a case fact. Same shape
// as `us.irs.rev_rul_afr` (phase 1).
//
// LAYOUT NOTE. `check_laws_tree` §3.5 derives `us/rev-rul-6621-quarterly`
// from jurisdiction US + instrument guidance (`us.irs` is not a
// GROUP_BY_NAME_PREFIX group): the package name keeps the `irs` issuer
// segment, the path does not — same as `us/rev-rul-afr`.
//
// OUT OF SCOPE. Monthly AFR rulings (in `us.irs.rev_rul_afr`); ruling
// text slices (later phase, old-PL scheme); anything beyond the four
// 2026 quarters.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irs.rev_rul_6621_quarterly version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irs:rev_rul_6621_quarterly:clir";
